ased on first impressions he  will freely admit when he's been proven  wrong and perhaps due to the fact that  he is a father of a young child he was  the character who was most resistant to  the idea of having students tag along  for dangerous missions in fact he can  initially come across as quite  judgmental but in reality it's just his  way of showing concern now in the manga  we've seen that rock lock is incredibly  confident in himself so much so that he  actually arcs and I tired to use his  quirk on him because rock rock believed  he could change the future and if you  want to know more about nite ize quirk  and how we can predict the future then  the link is in the description for that  video which i put out last week also  final thing i actually forgot to mention  this but his real name is Ken okay so  now we've reached the end of the ROC  clock explanation part of the video so  now we're gonna move on to the wider  discussion around his character but  first I'm gonna set out what I think and  I advise that you listen till the very  end because if you were to only listen  halfway I think it would probably skew  your interpretation of my opinion so to  begin  unlike completely fictional locations  like Hogwarts for example where there  are no black people for no discernible  reason my hero academia is set in Japan  by and large is generally generally not  a place you would find by people now  that being said whilst my fear academia  is set on earth it's not our earth it's  not our world that we live in is set in  the far far future meaning that there is  a sufficient gap in time between where  we currently live the world we live in  and where the story of my hair Academy  takes place that gap in time is so  significant that you can use it to  justify any change you want really and  this is another important thing it's not  to say that you should do that either  it's not to say that you should make  demographic changes to include more  people in your show I'